{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/2625-how-do-you-handle-courts-in-low-populated-freeholds","id":2625,"title":"How do you handle Courts in low populated Freeholds?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-04T08:05:47-08:00","id":2625,"title":"How do you handle Courts in low populated Freeholds?","content":"As I stated in the title, I have no idea how to work a court system in a freehold with say, under 30 changelings. Most of my games have a freehold populus of around 70 to 120 changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/652-jay-stewart","name":"Jay Stewart","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar652_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T10:06:58-08:00","id":2721,"title":"","content":"This is something that I've been working on actually. At first I had a lot of trouble with how to construct it but I think that is because I was thinking of the freehold in terms of potential politics like I would when creating a Kindred Domain.<br /> <br /> But I think that might be a mistake for smaller freeholds (ie apparently most freeholds). I think it becomes easier (at least for me) once you start to think about it as a support group first and foremost. so lets take, a small example of 17 changelings that belong to the Crystle Center, a freehold in Little Rock, Arkansas.<br /> <br /> <br /> The demographics could be:<br /> Winter: 4<br /> Spring: 5<br /> Summer: 2<br /> Autumn: 4<br /> and 3 courtless<br /> <br /> and there lets say there are 3 more who are not apart of the free hold but live in the area so there is contact.<br /> <br /> The Freehold is still rather young, about 50 years old and was started by the Spring courtier Emily Gold, an Oneirophysic who visited from boston and ended up rallying the Lost in the area so that they had purpose and weren't so afraid. Because of this spring has always held the most power. And 3 it's members were a few of the ones that she found first.<br /> <br /> For the first couple of years, through contacts made it so that others could choose one of the four courts through a &quot;neighboring&quot; freehold in texas and from that they made the free hold (at that time only 8 members strong)<br /> <br /> The free hold has marginally grown since then but for the most part the courts function as more of a buddy buddy type of thing within the freehold while the ruler holds all of the power. The ruler is chosen democratically within each court each time the season changes so there is only ever one ruler. It's pretty much always been Gold during Springs.<br /> <br /> How do they work if they are so small?<br /> Winter: three of them are good friends with the political mindset of hiding. They pretty much provide much of the support of the freehold. They provide homes and places of hiding. there really isn't much funds but they do what they do what they can.<br /> <br /> Spring: in charge of meet ups and events<br /> <br /> Summer: usually relies on Winter for help (intelligence) but for the most part they (known as the twins even though they arn't related in any way) provide defense for usually hedge related stuff.<br /> <br /> Autumn: the ones leaving for the hedge most often, most of them, however want to help the freehold integrate better with society, on that end they focus mostly on fetches which many of the members still have to deal with.<br /> <br /> The courtless are all apart of the Oneirophysics and so are 2 Winter courtiers. The Health is a pretty big deal in their group.<br /> <br /> <br /> So that's how I would build a Small member freehold/4 courts. in a support group/club kind of mindset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T10:19:21-08:00","id":2734,"title":"","content":"I'd say it works pretty much the same, albeit less hierarchic; instead of a sovereign surrounded by knights and nobles, each Court is just a boss and then the rest, with maybe one or two individuals with some kind of elevated position. The biggest difference would lie in the relationship <i>between</i> the Courts, since the small population leads to everyone in the freehold knowing everyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T13:24:56-08:00","id":2856,"title":"","content":"My key setting has several small freeholds with similarly small Courts. Each Court has a major focus, not just in its approach to living but in its performance for the freehold. Generally speaking, since they have so much to do and fewer people to do it with, Court members tend to be recognized more for their function than for their titles, and some folks serve multiple functions for the freehold.<br /> <br /> The Courts end up working together fairly often just to get things done, and there are fewer cliques to cause strife and/or to run away from the main freehold with. Court gatherings are more intimate, their response times tend to be more immediate, and politics are more personal than group-based.<br /> <br /> The philosophical differences that keep the freeholds apart lead them to run their Courts rather distinctively, so it is more common for the Spring Court of one freehold to disdain the Spring Court of another than it is for people within the same Spring Court to turn their noses up at one another.<br /> <br /> Additionally, while two freeholds have seasonal rulers, one does not, relying instead on freehold elders who make suggestions that are usually obeyed if only because they have been free for so long. All three freeholds rely on non-changelings, mortal and otherwise, ensorcelled or simply pledgebound, for many services.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":227,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","user":"KismetRose","date":". 11-05-2013, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T02:30:58-08:00","id":3310,"title":"","content":"Well one thing I am always inclined to do in my games is have Freeholds consider more then just changelings among their number. So Enchanted Mortals, and sometimes Fetches depending on the local opinions. And in some freeholds Mages and Ghosts. But a Freehold with less then say 20 Changelings would work, its more like a collection of Motleys, they may even be more inclined to just let one person stay king all year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T06:33:44-08:00","id":7305,"title":"","content":"I'm running a game with a freehold of about 20 changelings. 3 Summers, 9 Autumns, 6 Winters, and 4 Springs. Including PCs. The courts end up more like small clubs or cliques than real organizations. Each court still has its agenda, and its way of doing things, but it's more like like-minded friends than anything else. The MG describes about how it's turned out for me: Everyone knows everyone else, so the relationship between the courts is more intimate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/11I0xCPgAS3ZhxGvTlBoePOuaDqgpyWs13jVKhJ4c8hM/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Emerald Circle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/37100-white-elephant-for-flintlock-sidereal-custom-charms-and-discussion-on-themes\" target=\"_blank\">Custom Sidereal Charms</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sQxyi3ox0qn53c_vsUaVQi_pRdpKlQE50NT5ldQmxYI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Expanded Sidereal Linguistics</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/263-limited-reagent","name":"Limited Reagent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar263_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T08:12:16-08:00","id":7356,"title":"","content":"Another interesting thing to consider is what happens when new changelings show up. Politics probably aren't as big a deal in these smaller freeholds as they may be somewhere like miami, but in a freehold with four or five changelings per court, one or two new changelings can represent a real shift in the balance of power. How that's handled sort of comes down to what the other changelings in the freehold are like but it could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T16:04:35-08:00","id":7717,"title":"","content":"Imbalance. Our freehold is in a small area, a bunch of changelings were either wiped out or went into hiding when hunters started snatching them up. The freehold broke apart and in the end one person (summer court) essentially took charge and started a new one. While it would have been great if things went perfectly, there was no autumn court left to take over after summer. It didn't help that everyone was intimidated of him and still a bit shaken over the disappearance of the previous freehold. Eventually a new guy came, part of the Winter court, and there was a passing of power, and once we kill him we'll be trying to get things organized so that there's a more smooth and scheduled transition of power and a more organized representation of the various courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T04:05:59-08:00","id":7966,"title":"","content":"i had a game with a PC who was the highest ranking member of the court of the west in NYC such court was 4 guys in a chow fan restaurant whose turf was 4 blocks of chinatown with a &quot;official reunion&quot; once per month. And the other guys in the court took the court thing very seriously while my PC didnt give a fuck about it so it decend in funny scenarios like.<br /> <br /> -Sorry guys, im late i had a business to take care of.<br /> -You coming late endanger us all and is a breach of protocol and security. We have been sitting duck here and to come here we are leaving out turf un protected.<br /> *my pc would arch an eye brow, the procce to exit the chow fan restaurant. Look at both sided of the street and the go back in*<br /> -Ok, security check. No horde of invasor in the vecinities and our frontiers are secure- <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One way to go with low poblated freehold is that instead of courts having control each member is from a court by function and the free hold is like a big organization. The enforcers are the summer, the spies are the winter so on so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 1</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Assume players are bastards, bastard coated bastards with bastard filling until proven otherwise.</div> <div align=\"center\"><b><u>Rule number 2</u></b></div> <div align=\"center\">I don't care about the theme of personal horror.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/121-kaho","name":"kaho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T18:19:23-08:00","id":9368,"title":"","content":"In my game, the Freehold had an initial population of 28 Changelings. I purposefully went for a lopsided freehold, where Spring (which had 11 members) had an incredible amount of influence even when they weren't ruling. Winter had a measly four Changelings, all involved in a single polygamous relationship. Summer and Autumn had 7 and 6 members, respectively. Summer and Spring both then supplemented their power by bringing in large numbers of ensorcelled mortals to help guard the local trods. Each Court has a ruler, and then usually a lieutenant/enforcer figure. For the most part, there's hardly any internal politics within the Courts, but a lot of bickering. When we started, Winter was just taking power. With only four members though, the King found that most Changelings would look to their own Court Rulers first before following his commands, and the other Courts stepped up the politics by agreeing to follow his commands only when it suited them. They usually tried to convince Winter to offer them perks in return for following his orders. Spring was particularly troublesome, with their own rule just around the corner and their general attitude that they should always be in charge.<br /> <br /> As others have said, when you have low numbers of Changelings then power can swing rather drastically over only a few Changelings more or less in a given Court. Giving one Court a lot more members than any other is a good way to throw in some politics into a small Freehold. The increased manpower from the ensorcelled mortals provides some interesting options as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}